// A frame on a ranking function. rank() reads the whole partition by definition, so a frame has
// nothing to narrow, and the SQL standard bars the combination.
//
// Measured before this was refused: MariaDB, SQL Server, Oracle and Trino each rejected it with
// their own driver message; DuckDB, PostgreSQL and SQLite ignored the frame; and Snowflake accepted
// it and returned a DIFFERENT number — 2 where the others said 5. That last one is why this is an
// error and not a warning.
FIND orders o
FILTER o.order_id < 10253
FETCH o.order_id ASC,
      rank() OVER (ORDER o.freight ROWS BETWEEN 1 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) r
